---
// Figure: hit ratio and stale share of hits against TTL, for keys read at different rates.
import SimFigure from '../shared/SimFigure.astro';
import Choice from '../shared/Choice.astro';
import Readout from '../shared/Readout.astro';
import './figures.css';
interface Props { number: number }
const { number } = Astro.props;
---
<SimFigure number={number} id="ee-ttl-tradeoff" title="What a longer TTL buys, and what it costs" controls="none"
  caption="Illustrative model, not a measurement: the formulas derived above for one key whose database value changes once an hour on average, with reads arriving at random at the chosen rate. Nothing invalidates the copy on writes.">
  <Choice slot="params" name="rate" label="This product page is read" value="60"
    options={[{ value: '1', label: 'Once an hour' }, { value: '60', label: 'Once a minute' }, { value: '3600', label: 'Once a second' }]} />
  <Fragment slot="stats">
    <Readout name="needed" label="TTL for 90% hits" kind="hit" />
    <Readout name="stale" label="Stale hits at that TTL" kind="stale" />
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="text">
    <p>The chart plots two curves against the TTL, from zero to an hour. The stale share of hits rises almost in a straight line, to about 37% at one hour, and it is the same whichever read rate is chosen. The hit ratio depends on the read rate. Read once a second, the key passes 90% hits at a 9-second TTL, when about 0.1% of hits are stale. Read once a minute, it needs 9 minutes, when about 7% of hits are stale. Read once an hour, it reaches only 50% at a one-hour TTL and would need 9 hours for 90%, by which time most hits would be stale.</p>
  </Fragment>
</SimFigure>
<script>
  import { bindParams, setReadouts } from '../shared/player.mjs';
  import { lineChart } from '../shared/chart.mjs';
  import { hitRatio, staleShare, ttlForHitRatio } from './ttl-model.mjs';

  const CHANGE = 1 / 3600;
  const duration = (s: number) => (s < 90 ? `${Math.round(s)} s` : s < 5400 ? `${Math.round(s / 60)} min` : `${Math.round(s / 3600)} hours`);
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-figure-id="ee-ttl-tradeoff"]').forEach(root => {
    const chart = lineChart(root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-scene]')!, {
      label: 'Hit ratio and stale share of hits against TTL',
      height: 240,
      x: { label: 'TTL (minutes)', domain: [0, 60], format: (v: number) => String(v) },
      y: { label: 'Share', domain: [0, 1], format: (v: number) => `${Math.round(v * 100)}%` },
      series: [
        { id: 'hit', label: 'Hit ratio', kind: 'hit' },
        { id: 'stale', label: 'Hits that are stale', kind: 'stale' },
      ],
    });
    const stalePoints = Array.from({ length: 121 }, (_, i) => [i / 2, staleShare(CHANGE, i * 30)]);
    bindParams(root, params => {
      const rate = Number(params.rate) / 3600;
      chart.set('hit', Array.from({ length: 121 }, (_, i) => [i / 2, hitRatio(rate, i * 30)]));
      chart.set('stale', stalePoints);
      chart.render();
      const ttl = ttlForHitRatio(rate, 0.9);
      setReadouts(root, { needed: duration(ttl), stale: `${(staleShare(CHANGE, ttl) * 100).toFixed(staleShare(CHANGE, ttl) < 0.01 ? 1 : 0)}%` });
    });
  });
</script>
